            "Resolution": "1. Verify the DMM is seated properly.\n2. Examine gold fingers on edge of the DIMM to verify contacts are clean.\n3. Inspect the processor socket this DIMM is connected to for bent pins, and if found, replace the board.\n 4. Consider replacing the DIMM as a preventative measure. For multiple occurrences, replace the DIMM."
